        "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The conversation is summarized below:\nAnalysis:\nLet me chronologically analyze this conversation to ensure I capture all critical details:\n\n**Session Context:**\nThis is a continuation from a previous session that ran out of context. The user provided a detailed summary at the start.\n\n**User Messages:**\n1. Initial request: \"Please continue the conversation from where we left it off without asking the user any further questions. Continue with the last task that you were asked to work on.\"\n2. Summary request: Request for detailed summary following specific format\n\n**My Actions:**\n\n1. **Read new-product.json** - Confirmed 4 products from previous session (jcode, n8n-mcp, Ruflo, DeepSeek TUI)\n\n2. **Updated TODO list** - Marked QUESTION 2 research as in_progress\n\n3. **Researched QUESTION 2 (AI coding CLIs/terminal agents):**\n   - Read GitHub trending pages (Python, Rust, Go)\n   - Discovered agent-of-empires and entireio/cli\n   - Read releases pages for both to verify launch dates\n   - agent-of-empires: Latest release v0.12.0 on \"17 Feb\" - too old (outside 14-day window)\n   - entireio/cli: Could not verify launch date within 14 days\n   - Neither product qualified for inclusion\n\n4. **Updated TODO and rewrote new-product.json** - No changes to products, just progress recording\n\n5. **Started QUESTION 5 (AI tools for specific developer workflows):**\n   - Attempted multiple web searches for debugging, refactoring, test generation tools\n   - Hit rate limiting (MCP error -429) on web search\n   - Read Product Hunt homepage - found Rosentic: \"Catch when coding agents break each other before merge\"\n   - Read Hacker News newest page\n   - Read GitHub trending page again\n   - Attempted to verify Rosentic details via web search and found information about it\n\n**Key Finding:**\n- Rosentic is a cross-PR conflict detection tool for AI coding agents\n- Tool detects conflicts when multiple AI agents work in parallel\n- Was #5 on Product Hunt \"Top Products Launching Today\"\n- However, I could not verify the exact launch date to confirm it fits the 14-day window\n\n**Technical Details:**\n- Working with date constraint: products must be launched within 14 days before 2026-05-04\n- Research categories: 7 QUESTIONs covering different AI coding tool types\n- Deliverable: JSON file with product details\n\n**Current Status:**\n- QUESTION 1: Completed (no new products found)\n- QUESTION 2: Completed (no new qualifying products found)\n- QUESTION 5: In progress - found Rosentic but cannot verify launch date\n- Still need to complete QUESTIONS 7, 11, 14, 16\n- Then perform union, filter, sort, and finalize\n\nSummary:\n## 1. Primary Request and Intent\n\nThe user requested continuation of research from a previous session to:\n- Research newly launched AI coding tools from the last 14 days (before 2026-05-04)\n- Cover 7 specific categories of AI coding tools\n- Deliver results in `/home/runner/work/agentdaily/agentdaily/updates/2026-05-04/new-product.json`\n- The user explicitly stated: \"Please continue the conversation from where we left it off without asking the user any further questions. Continue with the last task that you were asked to work on.\"\n\nThe 7 research categories (QUESTIONs) are:\n1. **Full AI IDEs** (similar to Windsurf/Cursor) - not just autocomplete plugins\n2. **AI coding CLIs/terminal agents** (repo-aware, can run commands, can manage tasks)\n3. **AI tools for specific developer workflows** (debugging, refactoring, test generation, migration)\n4. **AI code agents with \"project-long memory\" or \"workspace memory\"** across sessions\n5. **Open-source AI coding agents** that can be self-hosted or run locally\n6. **AI coding tools that integrate into existing IDEs** (VS Code, JetBrains, Neovim)\n7. **AI agents for DevOps/workflow orchestration** (CI/CD, deployment, observability, incident response)\n\n## 2. Key Technical Concepts\n\n- **Model Context Protocol (MCP)**: Protocol for AI assistant integration\n- **Swarm Intelligence**: Multi-agent collaboration systems\n- **Vector Memory/Embeddings**: Semantic memory systems using HNSW indexing\n- **Terminal User Interface (TUI)**: CLI-based interactive coding agents\n- **Recursive Language Model (RLM)**: Parallel reasoning using smaller models\n- **Zero-trust Federation**: Cross-machine agent collaboration with security\n- **Goal-Oriented Action Planning (GOAP)**: AI planning using A* search\n- **OAuth Providers**: Multi-provider authentication (Claude, OpenAI, Gemini, Copilot)\n- **Git Worktrees**: Running parallel agents on different branches\n- **tmux**: Terminal multiplexer for session management\n- **Cross-PR Conflict Detection**: Detecting conflicts between multiple AI agents working in parallel\n- **14-Day Launch Window**: Products must be launched on or after 2026-04-20 (14 days before 2026-05-04)\n\n## 3. Files and Code Sections\n\n### `/home/runner/work/agentdaily/agentdaily/updates/2026-05-04/new-product.json`\n\n**Why Important**: This is the primary deliverable file containing research results about newly launched AI coding tools.\n\n**Current Contents**: 4 products from previous session (no changes made in this session):\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"jcode\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode\",\n    \"description\": \"A next-generation coding agent harness built for multi-session workflows with infinite customizability. Features semantic memory embeddings for project-long recall, swarm collaboration across multiple agents, browser automation via Firefox Agent Bridge, and exceptional performance (14ms to first frame, 167MB RAM). Supports OAuth providers (Claude, OpenAI, Gemini, Copilot, etc.) and self-dev mode where agents modify their own source code.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-04-20\",\n    \"category\": \"AI coding CLI\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub Trending\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"591 stars today with 3,418 total stars\",\n      \"Built for multi-session workflows, infinite customizability, and performance\",\n      \"6.0× more RAM efficient than alternatives in active sessions\",\n      \"Swarm mode enables native collaboration between multiple agents with conflict resolution\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"n8n-mcp\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/czlonkowski/n8n-mcp\",\n    \"description\": \"A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that gives AI assistants comprehensive access to n8n's workflow automation platform. Provides structured access to 1,650+ n8n nodes (820 core + 830 community), node properties, operations, and documentation. Enables Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf, and other AI IDEs to build, validate, and deploy n8n workflows with 99% property coverage and 2,352 searchable templates.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    \"category\": \"workflow agent\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub Trending\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"282 stars today with 19,511 total stars\",\n      \"A bridge between n8n's workflow automation platform and AI models\",\n      \"Supports 1,650 n8n nodes with 99% property coverage\",\n      \"Works with Claude Code, VS Code, Cursor, Windsurf, and Codex\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Ruflo\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/ruvnet/ruflo\",\n    \"description\": \"Multi-agent AI orchestration platform for Claude Code that coordinates 100+ specialized agents across machines and trust boundaries. Features self-learning swarm intelligence, HNSW-indexed vector memory (AgentDB), zero-trust federation for cross-machine agent collaboration, 32 Claude Code plugins, web UI at flo.ruv.io, and GOAP goal planner at goal.ruv.io. Agents self-organize, learn from tasks, and remember across sessions.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-04-25\",\n    \"category\": \"code agent\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub Trending\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"1,840 s